# Allowed signers for git commits in this repository.
#
# Policy: https://gitlab.moselwal.io/development/gitlab-profile/-/blob/main/igs/engineering/commit-signing-policy.md
# Standard: ed25519 signing key on YubiKey 5 Series, FIDO2 resident, verify-required.
#
# Format follows the OpenSSH allowed-signers convention and is consumed by
# `git verify-commit` and the commit-signing/verify CI gate:
#
#   <email-identity> namespaces="git" <ssh-public-key-or-gpg-fingerprint>
#
# One line per authorised signer. CODEOWNERS controls who can edit this file
# (same review pool as security-sensitive changes per the policy).
#
# To enrol (per engineer, once):
#   ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -O resident -O verify-required \
#     -C "you@moselwal.de" -f ~/.ssh/moselwal-signing
#   # Add the public key to your GitLab profile under "SSH signing keys"
#   # (the auth SSH key list is separate — GitLab distinguishes the usage).
#   # Then append one line below:
#   #   you@moselwal.de namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... you@moselwal.de
#
# GPG signing remains acceptable when paired with a YubiKey-resident GPG
# key already registered with GitLab; use the GPG fingerprint form on
# the line for that case.
